## [Managing your purchase orders](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/awsaccountbilling/latest/aboutv2/manage-purchaseorders.md)

- [Setting up purchase order configurations](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/awsaccountbilling/latest/aboutv2/setup-po-lineitem.md): Set up your purchase orders for your AWS account.
- [Adding a purchase order](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/awsaccountbilling/latest/aboutv2/adding-po.md): Add a purchase order for your AWS account
- [Editing your purchase orders](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/awsaccountbilling/latest/aboutv2/edit-po.md): You can edit your purchase order, line item information, and status using the Billing and Cost Management console.
- [Deleting your purchase orders](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/awsaccountbilling/latest/aboutv2/delete-po.md): You can use the Billing and Cost Management console to delete your purchase order at any time, along with all of its notifications and associated contacts.
- [Viewing your purchase orders](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/awsaccountbilling/latest/aboutv2/viewing-po.md): Your purchase order dashboard on the Billing and Cost Management console shows you the state of your purchase orders at a glance.
- [Reading your purchase order details page](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/awsaccountbilling/latest/aboutv2/reading-po-details.md): You can review the contents of your individual purchase orders on the Purchase order details page of the Billing and Cost Management console.
- [Enabling purchase order notifications](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/awsaccountbilling/latest/aboutv2/notify-po-details.md): Enable purchase order notifications for your AWS account.
- [Use tags to manage access to purchase orders](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/awsaccountbilling/latest/aboutv2/manage-access-to-purchase-orders-with-tags.md): You can add tags to your purchase orders and then use IAM policies to allow or deny access to them.


## [Explore AWS services with AWS Free Tier](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/awsaccountbilling/latest/aboutv2/free-tier.md)

- [Choosing a plan](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/awsaccountbilling/latest/aboutv2/free-tier-plans.md): Learn the difference between free account plan and paid plan for your AWS Free Tier.
- [Earning additional credits](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/awsaccountbilling/latest/aboutv2/free-tier-plans-activities.md): If you are a new AWS customer, you can earn an additional USD $100 in credits regardless of your account plan by completing activities.
- [Track your usage](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/awsaccountbilling/latest/aboutv2/tracking-free-tier-usage.md): Track your AWS Free Tier service usage for your AWS account.
- [Avoiding unexpected charges after Free Tier](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/awsaccountbilling/latest/aboutv2/avoid-charges-after-free-tier.md): Avoid unexpected charges after the AWS Free Tier expires for your AWS account.
- [Using the Free Tier API](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/awsaccountbilling/latest/aboutv2/using-free-tier-api.md): Use the Free Tier API to programmatically get your free tier usage.


## [Organizing costs using AWS Cost Categories](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/awsaccountbilling/latest/aboutv2/manage-cost-categories.md)

- [Creating cost categories](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/awsaccountbilling/latest/aboutv2/create-cost-categories.md): Create cost categories to allocate costs in your business..
- [Tagging cost categories](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/awsaccountbilling/latest/aboutv2/tag-cost-categories.md): How to tag your cost categories.
- [Viewing cost categories](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/awsaccountbilling/latest/aboutv2/view-cost-categories.md): View and download comprehensive information about your AWS Billing and Cost Management category details and values using the cost category details page.
- [Downloading your cost category values](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/awsaccountbilling/latest/aboutv2/view-cost-categories-details-csv.md): You can download an offline copy of your month-to-date cost category spend from your cost category dashboard details page.
- [Editing cost categories](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/awsaccountbilling/latest/aboutv2/edit-cost-categories.md): How to edit your cost categories.
- [Deleting cost categories](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/awsaccountbilling/latest/aboutv2/delete-cost-categories.md): How to delete your cost categories.
- [Splitting charges within cost categories](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/awsaccountbilling/latest/aboutv2/splitcharge-cost-categories.md): Use split charge rules to allocate charges between your cost category values.
- [Using cost categories with other services](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/awsaccountbilling/latest/aboutv2/cost-categories-other-cost-management.md): Learn how to use cost category with other cost management and optimization tools


## [Organizing and tracking costs using AWS cost allocation tags](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/awsaccountbilling/latest/aboutv2/cost-alloc-tags.md)

### [Using AWS-generated tags](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/awsaccountbilling/latest/aboutv2/aws-tags.md)

Learn about AWS-generated tags.

- [Activating AWS-generated tags cost allocation tags](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/awsaccountbilling/latest/aboutv2/activate-built-in-tags.md): Learn how to activate the AWS-generated tags.
- [Deactivating the AWS-generated tags cost allocation tags](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/awsaccountbilling/latest/aboutv2/deactivate-built-in-tags.md): Learn how to deactivate the AWS-generated tags.

### [Using user-defined cost allocation tags](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/awsaccountbilling/latest/aboutv2/custom-tags.md)

User-defined tags are tags that you define, create, and apply to resources.

- [Activating user-defined cost allocation tags](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/awsaccountbilling/latest/aboutv2/activating-tags.md): Activate cost allocation tags for your AWS Billing reports.
- [Using user attributes for cost allocation](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/awsaccountbilling/latest/aboutv2/user-attributes-cost-allocation.md): Learn how to use user attributes for cost allocation with AWS applications.
- [Using account tags for cost allocation](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/awsaccountbilling/latest/aboutv2/account-tags-cost-allocation.md): Learn how to use account tags for cost allocation with AWS applications.
- [Using IAM principal for cost allocation](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/awsaccountbilling/latest/aboutv2/iam-principal-cost-allocation.md): Use IAM principal identity and tags to track AWS costs for Amazon Bedrock by caller identity across applications and organizational structures.
- [Backfill cost allocation tags](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/awsaccountbilling/latest/aboutv2/cost-allocation-backfill.md): You can request a backfill of cost allocation tags for up to 12 months.
- [Using the monthly cost allocation report](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/awsaccountbilling/latest/aboutv2/configurecostallocreport.md): Set up and customize your monthly cost allocation report for your AWS usage to see meaningful billing information that helps you track your costs.
- [Understanding dates for cost allocation tags](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/awsaccountbilling/latest/aboutv2/cost-allocation-tags-timeline.md): You can determine when you last used or updated your cost allocation tags.


