## [Consolidating billing for AWS Organizations](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/awsaccountbilling/latest/aboutv2/consolidated-billing.md)

- [Consolidated billing process](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/awsaccountbilling/latest/aboutv2/useconsolidatedbilling-procedure.md): AWS Organizations provides consolidated billing so that you can track the combined costs of all the member accounts in your organization.
- [Consolidated billing in AWS EMEA](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/awsaccountbilling/latest/aboutv2/consolidated-billing-emea.md): Consolidate your AWS account bills in Amazon Web Services EMEA SARL (AWS Europe).
- [Consolidated billing in India](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/awsaccountbilling/latest/aboutv2/useconsolidatedbilling-India.md): If you sign up for a new account and choose India for your contact and billing address, your user agreement is with Amazon Web Services India Private Limited (AWS India), a local AWS seller in India.
- [Effective billing date, account activity, and volume discounts](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/awsaccountbilling/latest/aboutv2/useconsolidatedbilling-effective.md): When the member account owner accepts your request to join the organization, you immediately become responsible for the member account's charges.

### [Reserved Instances](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/awsaccountbilling/latest/aboutv2/ri-behavior.md)

For billing purposes, the consolidated billing feature of AWS Organizations treats all the accounts in the organization as one account.

- [Billing examples for specific services](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/awsaccountbilling/latest/aboutv2/consolidatedbilling-other.md): There are a few other things to know about how consolidated billing works with specific services in AWS.
- [Reserved Instances and Savings Plans discount sharing](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/awsaccountbilling/latest/aboutv2/ri-turn-off.md): Activate or deactivate and share Reserved Instance and Amazon Simple Pay for accounts in your organization.
- [Understanding Consolidated Bills](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/awsaccountbilling/latest/aboutv2/con-bill-blended-rates.md): If you manage an organization in AWS Organizations, you can use consolidated billing to view aggregated usage costs for accounts in the organization.
- [Requesting shorter PDF invoices](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/awsaccountbilling/latest/aboutv2/consolidated-invoice-summary-options.md): You can request PDF invoices that are shorter and have fewer member account details.
- [Organization support charges](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/awsaccountbilling/latest/aboutv2/consolidatedbilling-support.md): AWS calculates Support fees independently for each member account.


